(d) The notice of assessment serves as the notification of the approval, approval in part, or disapproval of the claim for exemption. If the claim for exemption is disapproved by the director, the claimant may appeal the disapproval pursuant to § 8-12.1.

(e) Upon the director’s approval of the initial claim for an exemption, the exemption will continue for a period of 20 consecutive years; provided that the owner annually certifies that in the preceding tax year, the film studio facility or its users:

(1) Promoted local workforce development in the field of motion picture, film, and digital media by partnering with its film-lease production companies, studio partners, and other users of the film studio facility to provide paid on-set production or post-production internship programs arranged with local colleges, universities, or vocational schools for their students who are pursuing a degree or career in film or media studies, or to provide on-set, production, or post-production apprenticeships;

