- Are necessary for providing and preserving parklands, wilderness, and beach reserves, and for conserving natural ecosystems of indigenous and endemic plants, invertebrates, fish and wildlife, for forestry, and other activities related to these uses;
- Are located at an elevation below the maximum inland line of the zone of wave action, and marine waters, fishponds, and tide pools unless otherwise designated;
- Are generally characterized by topography, soils, climate or other related environmental factors that may not be normally adaptable or presently needed for urban or agriculture use;
- Have general slopes of 20 percent or more and which provide for open space amenities and/or scenic values;
